  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Reconciliation Book",
    "overview": "The console is kept like a merchant's account book. A bookcloth-green rail binds the left edge; the page is pale ruled ledger paper; text is blue-black ink; refusals post in red ink with parenthesised amounts and the rule code as the memo; totals close on a double rule. Every surface reads as an entry, a statement or a column of figures, never as a grid of KPI tiles.\n\nDensity is working-office density: 15px body, tight table rows, hairline seams between panels, and figures set tabular everywhere so columns add up by eye. Serif carries the statement voice (page titles, the dashboard headline sentence, flow-page questions); a workhorse sans carries every control and label; mono carries references, rule codes and version strings.\n\nLight and dark share one token set: a `prefers-color-scheme: dark` block swaps every value, so components only ever reference tokens.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Bookcloth rail, ruled paper ground, hairline seams, no drop shadows.",
      "Four state inks (green allow, red block, amber reauthorise, blue review), each with a tinted ground.",
      "Ledger tables with uppercase tracked column heads, faint vertical column rules and a double-ruled total.",
      "Serif for statements, sans for operation, mono for references.",
      "Tabular lining figures on the body element, not opt-in."
